findings.body:
**A package with no dependencies and its own lockfile is now always refused.**

The JSDoc says the refusal is for a package "the trusted manifest gives a dependency". But the code only lets a package through on the hoisted-member branch, and it skips that branch whenever the package holds its own lockfile (`lock.dir === pkg.dir`). A package with an empty `declared` set therefore falls through to the `throw`:

```ts
const declared = { ...manifest.dependencies, ...manifest.devDependencies };
const lock = nearestLockfile(repoPath, pkg.dir);
if (
  lock?.dir !== pkg.dir &&
  Object.keys(declared).every((name) => existsSync(join(repoPath, GATE_ENVIRONMENT_DIR, name)))
) {
  return;
}
```

**Trigger:** `tools/x/package.json` is `{"scripts":{"test":"node --test"}}` with a committed `tools/x/package-lock.json`.

- The adapter gives it a `test` command, because commands come only from scripts (`typescript.adapter.ts:577-586`). So the `pkg.commands.length === 0` return doesn't fire.
- `npm install` on a manifest with no dependencies writes the lockfile but creates no `node_modules` (medium: npm behaviour).
- A branch touching `tools/x/` throws "Install it with `npm --prefix tools/x install`". Running that install changes nothing, so every later merge is refused the same way.

Before this PR, `linkEnvironment` returned quietly and `node --test` passed. When no lockfile exists anywhere, the empty `every` returns true and the package passes. So only the own-lockfile case breaks, and no test covers it: every refusal test declares `vitest`.

https://github.com/AlexisBalayre/pupitre/blob/8d45bde62cd071b0f4a44b846719ff0cb202e432/src/core/merge-gate.service.ts#L1560-L1569

findings.suggestion:
const declared = Object.keys({ ...manifest.dependencies, ...manifest.devDependencies });
if (declared.length === 0) return;
const lock = nearestLockfile(repoPath, pkg.dir);
// Only a member, with no lockfile of its own, has its dependencies hoisted,
// and of the directories above it the gate links the root's alone.
if (
  lock?.dir !== pkg.dir &&
  declared.every((name) => existsSync(join(repoPath, GATE_ENVIRONMENT_DIR, name)))
) {
  return;
}
